# Commits that changed only formatting, which `git blame` should look through.
#
# 🖌️ Code Style Formatter lands its fixes as format-only commits. Without
# this file, every line it touched blames that commit instead of the change
# that actually wrote the line. GitHub's blame view reads this file from the
# root of the repository on its own; for the command line, run once:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Add the full 40-character SHA of a commit that changed formatting and
# nothing else, one per line, with a comment naming it. Never list a commit
# that also changed behaviour: blame would hide who wrote that behaviour.
